      level: "class1",
      assumptions: "Fictional system in western Canada: resamples = 12, total samples = 960. Percent equals resamples divided by total, times 100. Provincial drinking water requirements and the Guidelines for Canadian Drinking Water Quality frame the context in general terms.",
